# Quantify Resume Impact

Every experience bullet must contain at least one concrete metric. ATS checkers flag task-only bullets.

## Formula

`[strong verb] [what you built/owned] so that [measurable result].`

Valid metrics (prefer the strongest you can honestly support):

- Outcomes: conversion, revenue, load time, bounce rate, acquisition
- Scale: users, merchants, regions, transactions, $ volume
- Efficiency: time saved, fewer steps, faster onboarding, fewer incidents

## Rules

- Never invent numbers. If a metric is missing, ask the user for it before writing the bullet.
- Do not ship placeholders like `[X%]` or "significantly improved" in the live resume.
- Vague intensifiers (`significantly`, `frictionless`, `robust`, `seamless`) do not count as quantification.
- Scope numbers are acceptable when outcome data does not exist yet (e.g. a new role): `2 payment providers`, `3 regions`, `N merchants`.
- Keep bullets to one sentence and roughly 1–2 lines.

## Examples

```
❌ Architected and executed full-stack migration from legacy infrastructure to a modern React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Express.js stack deployed on Railway.
✅ Migrated the platform from legacy infrastructure to React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Express on Railway, cutting average page load from 4.2s to 1.1s.

❌ Led the end-to-end rebuild of the corporate web portal, significantly improving brand positioning, site performance, and user acquisition.
✅ Rebuilt the corporate web portal, lifting organic sign-ups 28% and dropping bounce rate from 61% to 39%.
```
